  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Afghanistan - MIDO Dairy: Training local youth how to process dairy in Kabul.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MIDO Dairy in Kabul, Afghanistan focusses on dairy processing and producing products such as yoghurt for local consumption. Although there is dairy production in Afghanistan, fresh dairy products are rare and 90% of dairy products are imported from nearby countries such as Iran. Vocational training or education for this field is not available in the country and people are usually trained on the job.  With the support of Technical Assistance (DGGF), the company sought to increase local production capacity, to improve the local supply chain and milk quality and to enable local sourcing of milk by transferring knowledge. Part of the project was the purchase of milk testing equipment, local sourcing of milk through implementing cooled transport and providing training and coaching to local youth and milk farmers. The project directly supported 21 jobs and indirectly supported 50 milk farmers. 27 employees of MIDO received training on how to produce high quality milk products and 50 farmers were educated on how to increase milk quality and hygiene. Furthermore, an additional 800 store owners received regular awareness coaching on how to cold store fresh dairy products in order to maintain product quality. Further upscaling activities are currently being explored.</narrative>
  </description>
